# ── Rust & Tauri Desktop ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
.tauri/target/
.tauri/gen/
gen/
# Cargo.lock is deliberately tracked. This is an application, not a library, and
# without it CI resolves the Rust graph from scratch on every run. That is how
# the desktop bundle broke with nobody touching a dependency: tauri-plugin-updater
# 2.12.0 landed upstream, the unpinned crate requirement picked it up, and Tauri
# then refused to build against the 2.11.0 npm package. The npm side has always
# been pinned by package-lock.json; this is the same guarantee for the crate side.
**/*.rs.bk

# ── Python Runtime & Tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

